Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=(), event=Decided(decision='calendarplugin', at=datetime(2026, 10, 24, 0, 0, 0), actor='assistant', title='The calendar is the first plugin; its schema is a declaration, its store is cache tier, and its titles are tainted', body="*The calendar is the first* (`app/plugin-ics`, on the `icalendar` parser and `rrule`; `suzatary_core::calendar`): `sync` is lent the NAMES of the credentials its manifest declares (a calendar's secret iCal link, `PLUGIN_ICS_*`, asked for by the box's own card, never in a chat), and what it emits enters only through its schema's door. *A plugin's schema is a DECLARATION*: `[[plugins]] schema` names its text beside the component (`app/plugin-ics/ics.schema`; no Rust schema mirrors it), admitted by the Prodrome's eight laws when the host loads it or the plugin is refused by the law it breaks; an item is an event of it (`plugin::admit`: parsed, printed back the same, written as the plugin itself), learned through `store::learn` (only what the store does not already read, so its 15-minute timer, `suzatary plugin sync`, takes no lock). Each plugin's store is CACHE tier, `cache/plugins/<name>/store` under the data root, its schema's text beside it: box-local, never pushed, never staged by `safe-push.sh` (a guard test), rebuilt by syncing again. The calendar is the READER of every such store whose schema has its registers. Its titles are other people's words, as mail is: the secretary's `calendar` verb is Tainted and `context`, which is Clean, carries none of it, so an invite's title can never reach the memory. Meetings are never todos; nothing writes from the calendar to a chain. The `actor` world, a plugin that only proposes, is kept as an interface (`app/wit/actor.wit`) and nothing hosts it until a plugin needs it.", rationale='Decided 2026-10-24, with the plugins.', supersedes=()))